# Line endings — see issue #150.
#
# This repo previously held a mix of CRLF and LF: 43 tracked source files were
# CRLF while the rest were LF, and lib/services/OpenAPIService.js was
# internally mixed (26 CRLF lines among 867 LF). Any tool that rewrites a file
# wholesale — sed -i, eslint --fix, tsc — would silently renormalise the whole
# file, turning a small edit into a diff of hundreds of lines and burying the
# real change.
#
# text=auto lets git classify text vs binary; eol=lf checks text out as LF on
# every platform, so the working tree matches the repository and no tool can
# introduce a spurious ending change. Node, npm, git and every editor in use
# handle LF on Windows without issue.
#
# Related: tsconfig.json sets "newLine": "lf" so compiled output is LF
# regardless of the source file's endings. Without it, a single CRLF source
# would emit CRLF and show up as build drift in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never classified, diffed, or converted.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
